# 2. Secured and monitored web infrastructure

Website: www.foobar.com (served over HTTPS)
The `www` record (A record) points to the IP of the load balancer.

## Infrastructure

- 3 servers:
  - 1 load balancer server: firewall, HAProxy, SSL certificate for
    www.foobar.com, monitoring client
  - 2 identical application servers (Server 1 and Server 2), each with:
    firewall, web server (Nginx), application server, code base, MySQL
    database, monitoring client
- 3 firewalls (one per server)
- 1 SSL certificate (www.foobar.com), installed on the load balancer
- 3 monitoring clients (one per server), sending data to a monitoring
  service (for example Sumo Logic)
- The MySQL database of Server 1 is the Primary node, the one of Server 2 is
  the Replica node.

## What happens when a user visits https://www.foobar.com

1. The browser asks the DNS for the IP of www.foobar.com and gets the IP of
   the load balancer.
2. The browser opens an encrypted HTTPS connection to the load balancer. The
   firewall of the load balancer server only lets ports 80 and 443 through.
3. HAProxy uses the SSL certificate to decrypt the request, then chooses a
   server (Round Robin) and forwards it to that server through its firewall.
